    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_5",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Anne Emily Innes-Ker, Duchess of Roxburghe {'1': \", '2': \", '3': \", '4': \"} (\"née\" Spencer-Churchill; 14 November 1854 – 20 June 1923) was the daughter of the 7th Duke of Marlborough, who served in Conservative governments as Lord President of the Council and Lord Lieutenant of Ireland. She served as Mistress of the Robes to Queen Victoria.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
